ATTRIBUTION: THE ID TABLES

Each table in data/ is a small slice of a public source, pinned by the sha256 in data/pins.json.
They are used here to check LINK answers. The upstream sources and their licenses:

  release.MONDO.jsonl
      Mondo Disease Ontology ids (Monarch Initiative), https://mondo.monarchinitiative.org/
      A first slice was retrieved through the EMBL-EBI Ontology Lookup Service (OLS), with Mondo's
      labels and synonyms; Mondo is licensed CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
      Most rows were added from Wikidata (see below): Mondo ids as Wikidata records them, with
      Wikidata's labels.

  release.ORPHA.jsonl
      Orphanet ids (ORPHAcodes), https://www.orpha.net/, as Wikidata records them, with Wikidata's
      labels (see below).

  release.CHEMBL.jsonl, release.RXCUI.jsonl, release.UNII.jsonl
      Wikidata, https://www.wikidata.org/ (the Wikidata Query Service).
      The ids are those of ChEMBL, RxNorm and the FDA Unique Ingredient Identifier, as Wikidata
      records them; the labels and synonyms are Wikidata's.
      License: CC0 1.0 for structured data, https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing

  release.UNIPROT.jsonl
      UniProt (the UniProt Consortium), https://www.uniprot.org/
      License: CC BY 4.0, https://www.uniprot.org/help/license

The tables are adapted: each row keeps only an id, its label, whether it is obsolete, and its
synonyms. No endorsement by any upstream source is implied.
